# STEP 5 — see README §5.
#
# The whole reverse proxy and TLS configuration is three lines. Caddy obtains
# and renews Let's Encrypt certificates on its own, provided:
#
#   - the site block names the real domains, apex and www;
#   - port 80 is reachable, because the ACME HTTP-01 challenge uses it;
#   - the certificates survive a restart, which is the volume in the compose
#     file rather than anything in here.
#
# Proxy to the api service by its compose service name and port. Do not name a
# container: service names are what Docker's embedded DNS resolves inside the
# network, and container names are global and collide.
#
